# BMW iX3 G08 five-door electric SUV, 2020 onwards.
#
# The electric X3: the closed kidney grille with blue trim, the smooth
# underbody, the iX3 rear badge and no exhaust outlets. UK pre-orders from
# November 2020, deliveries from summer 2021. The facelifted rear view in the
# pack is noted against the pre-facelift front and side.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_iX3
#
# Dimensions 4.734 x 1.891 x 1.668 m, wheelbase 2.864 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side profile exists. Image 1 is the most
# side-on view; the front and rear three-quarters show the closed grille and
# the tail. The flank is estimated; the facelift mismatch is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (c), provisional; no launch paint list was verified. Black,
# white, blue and grey are plain names. Weights 9, 8, 7, 6, total 30,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 180 km/h (electronically limited). Comfort 100/330, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 100: a quiet electric cabin. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2021 intro, retires staggered 2041-2044.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-ix3.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-ix3.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bmw-ix3/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear window is small, the shoulder crease is faint,
# and the black wheel-arch cladding is omitted. The tail-lamp graphic is the
# facelift form from image 3 on a pre-facelift body, the pack's known mismatch.
# Mirrors project beyond the published width. At 128 px the closed blue-ringed
# kidney grille, blue sill accent and smooth no-exhaust tail read as an iX3.


